flowchart TD
    Req([Runway Allocation Request: Flight F, Aircraft A]) --> LockRes[Acquire ResourceManager std::mutex]
    
    LockRes --> FilterRunways[Query All Runways Registered in Airport]
    FilterRunways --> LoopRunways{Iterate Each Runway}

    LoopRunways -- Done / None Valid --> UnlockFail[Release std::mutex]
    UnlockFail --> RejectAlloc([Return: Allocation Failed - No Compatible Runway])

    LoopRunways -- Check Next Runway R --> CheckStatus{Status == FREE?}
    CheckStatus -- No (OCCUPIED/MAINTENANCE) --> LoopRunways
    
    CheckStatus -- Yes --> CheckLength{Length >= Required for Wake Category?}
    CheckLength -- No --> LoopRunways

    CheckLength -- Yes --> CheckSurface{Surface Compatible with Aircraft?}
    CheckSurface -- No --> LoopRunways

    CheckSurface -- Yes --> SelectRunway[Select Candidate Runway R]
    SelectRunway --> AtomicLock[Mark Runway R as RESERVED in Memory]
    AtomicLock --> OpenTx[Start Database Transaction]

    OpenTx --> DBRowLock[SELECT status FROM runways WHERE id=R.id FOR UPDATE]
    DBRowLock --> DBStatusCheck{DB Status == 'FREE'?}

    DBStatusCheck -- No --> AbortTx[Rollback Database Transaction]
    AbortTx --> ResetMem[Revert Runway R to FREE in Memory]
    ResetMem --> LoopRunways

    DBStatusCheck -- Yes --> ExecStatements[Execute Allocation SQL Sequence:<br/>1. UPDATE flights SET status<br/>2. INSERT INTO runway_assignments<br/>3. UPDATE runways SET status='OCCUPIED'<br/>4. UPDATE scheduling_queue]

    ExecStatements --> CheckSQLOk{All SQL Statements Succeeded?}
    CheckSQLOk -- No --> AbortTx
    
    CheckSQLOk -- Yes --> CommitTx[COMMIT Database Transaction]
    CommitTx --> FinalizeMem[Mark Runway R as OCCUPIED in Memory]
    FinalizeMem --> UnlockSuccess[Release std::mutex]
    UnlockSuccess --> GrantAlloc([Return: Allocation Succeeded])
